            "review_title": "Review at Minh Tam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Kevin S\nNew York City, New York48 contributions\n0\nGive it a try if you love Vietnamese noodles\nDec 2015 • Family\nWe just walked passed by the little noodle shop and was attracted by the delicious smell from the soup in the large pods. So we walked back and ordered a beef noodle soup. It was so good that we ordered another pork rib noodle soup. Both were excellent, the best we've had in Vietnam so far. The shop is very clean, run by a nice lady. Portion was not generous however quality is top notch. Each noodle soup is a combination of chicken soup, beef bone and pork bone soup, very tasty. Highly recommend for a visit. It is on the main road on Nguyen Van Thoai, on the way from Cau Tran Thi Ly bridge to the beach. Apparently this is its first review on trip advisor so it must be a hidden gem. We've been searching for good Vietnamese noodles and this is first class.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 30, 2015",
